#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Phase gates {#phase-gates}"
msgstr "Gates de fase {#phase-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**T gate**\n"
msgstr "**Gate T**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The T gate is equivalent to RZ for the angle $\\pi/4$. Fault-tolerant "
"quantum computers will compile all quantum programs down to just the T gate "
"and its inverse, as well as the Clifford gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"O gate T é equivalente a RZ para o ângulo $\\pi/4$. Computadores quânticos "
"tolerantes a falhas compilarão todos os programas quânticos reduzindo-os "
"apenas ao gate T e seu inverso, bem como aos gates de Clifford.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![t\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/b5f1b90c-d3b7-4f60-82f9-259dc40cef5b.avif) | `t q[0];`          | ![image29](/docs/images/guides/composer/c43496bb-89ff-4518-9afb-d276e400b032.avif)                              | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
